So I was tweaking my .nethackrc, right, and started an explore-mode
game in order to test the results. Once I'd got it the way I wanted
it, I thought, well, since I'm sitting here in explore mode with a
half-empty WoW and some time to kill, why don't I whistle up a
couple of other useful things and see how much better than usual I
can do with that initial boost? So I carried on playing.

Eventually I was in a position to begin bulk armour enchantment, so
I took off most of my armour in order to enchant the right bits by
the right amount. Midway through this process an ettin mummy
surprised me, and managed to kill me before I could kill it. Well,
that's OK, I thought: this is explore mode, so I don't have to die
if I don't want to.

Except that I absentmindedly hit `y' at the `Die? [yn]' prompt.

There are any number of ways to get killed by failing to anticipate
dangers, or by doing something you didn't realise would kill you,
but I think accidentally answering `yes' to `do you want to die?'
has a YASD quality all of its own. Beat that!
